    "title": "Drue Tranquill injury update: Latest status report, news for KC Chiefs LB in Week 2 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By John Dillon ,\n48 minutes ago [US, Mexico & Canada customers only] Sep 5, 2025; Sao Paulo, BRAZIL; Los Angeles Chargers running back Omarion Hampton (8) runs against Kansas City Chiefs linebacker Drue Tranquill (23) in the second half during a NFL game at Corinthians Arena. Mandatory Credit: Amanda Perobelli/Reuters via Imagn Images By Amanda Perobelli, REUTERS Veteran linebacker Drue Tranquill was one of the Kansas City Chiefs ' most productive players in Week 1, but was listed on the team's injury report ahead of its matchup against the Philadelphia Eagles on September 14.\nTake a look at the latest update on Tranquill's status ahead of the Super Bowl LIX rematch:\nDrue Tranquill injury update Tranquill has been dealing with a back injury, but it hasn't affected his ability to participate in practice. He was a full participant in Kansas City's workouts on Wednesday.\nHow long will Drue Tranquill be out? For now, it seems likely that Tranquill will play against the Eagles. If his back injury doesn't flare up this week, he should be ready to take the field on Sunday.\nChiefs LB depth chart Rookie linebacker Jeffrey Bassa is listed as Tranquill's backup on Kansas City's unofficial depth chart, though veteran Jack Cochrane should also be available to fill in, if needed.\nThis article originally appeared on Chiefs Wire: Drue Tranquill injury update: Latest status report, news for KC Chiefs LB in Week 2",
